1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
Do you love food?
你热爱美食吗？

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:08,720
Whether you’re a foodie or someone who just likes eating, there is so much to choose from.
无论你是美食家，还是仅仅喜欢美食的人，可供选择的食物都有很多。

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:24,380
We know that too much of the wrong kind of food can be bad for our health, but for some people having a food allergy means eating certain things can actually be harmful - and now, it seems, this is affecting more and more of us.
我们都知道，过量食用不健康的食物会损害健康，但对一些有食物过敏症的人来说，吃某些食物其实是有危害的——而且如今，受这个问题影响的人似乎越来越多。

4
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:34,110
An allergy is caused by the immune system fighting substances in the environment, known as allergens, that it should see as harmless.
过敏是免疫系统攻击环境中本应被视为无害物质（即过敏原）而引发的。

5
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:46,750
Food allergies can cause life-threatening reactions, which means people have to spend their lives following strict dietary restrictions and worrying about the ingredients of everything they consume.
食物过敏可能会引发危及生命的反应，这意味着患者一生都要遵守严格的饮食限制，还要时刻担心自己所吃的每一样东西的成分。

6
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:57,920
Allergy specialist Dr Adam Fox says “if you look back over, say, 30 or 40 years… there are much more allergic problems around now than there were.”
过敏专科医生亚当·福克斯博士表示：“回顾过去三四十年，不难发现现在的过敏问题比以往多得多。”

7
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:03,100
We often hear about people having allergies to dairy products and to peanuts.
我们经常听说有人对乳制品和花生过敏。

8
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:11,700
Last year a 15-year-old girl died after suffering a fatal allergic reaction from eating a baguette containing sesame seeds.
去年，一名15岁女孩因食用含有芝麻的法棍面包引发致命过敏反应而死亡。

9
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,450
This led to a call for better food-labelling laws.
这一事件引发了人们对完善食品标签法规的呼吁。

10
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:20,480
Research has found that this problem is particularly affecting children.
研究发现，这个问题对儿童的影响尤为明显。

11
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:25,470
More and more of them are having allergic reactions to certain foodstuffs.
越来越多的儿童会对某些食物产生过敏反应。

12
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:39,150
Writing for the BBC website, Dr Alexandra Santos from King's College London says “food allergy now affects about 7% of children in the UK and 9% of those in Australia, for example.
伦敦国王学院的亚历山德拉·桑托斯博士在为英国广播公司网站撰稿时表示：“例如，目前英国约有7%的儿童、澳大利亚约有9%的儿童患有食物过敏症。

13
00:01:39,150 --> 00:01:43,150
Across Europe, 2% of adults have food allergies.”
在整个欧洲，有2%的成年人存在食物过敏问题。”

14
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:45,700
So what might be the cause?
那么，造成这种现象的原因可能是什么呢？

15
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:58,260
Dr Santos says the increase in allergies is not simply the effect of society becoming more aware of them and better at diagnosing them; it seems to be more environmental.
桑托斯博士表示，过敏症患者增多，不仅仅是因为社会对过敏的认知度提高、诊断水平有所进步，这一现象似乎更多与环境因素有关。

16
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:09,300
She says possible factors are “pollution, dietary changes and less exposure to microbes, which change how our immune systems respond.”
她指出，可能的诱因包括“污染、饮食变化以及接触微生物的机会减少，这些因素都会改变人体免疫系统的反应方式”。

17
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:19,050
She points out that it’s very common for migrants who move to another country to develop asthma and food allergies in their new location.
她还提到，移居他国的移民在新的生活地患上哮喘和食物过敏症，是十分常见的情况。

18
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:24,090
A lot of work is being done to try and find a cure, but that’s not easy.
目前，人们正在投入大量精力寻找治愈过敏的方法，但这并非易事。

19
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:31,120
So for now allergy sufferers must watch what they eat and they must rely on clear and accurate labelling.
因此，就现阶段而言，过敏患者必须格外留意自己的饮食，同时还要依赖清晰准确的食品标签。
